ppe-ros2 NOTICE

Model
  ppe_yolov8s_320_int8dyn.onnx (not stored in this repository; fetched at build
  time from https://zulfaqarhafez.com/models/ppe/ppe_yolov8s_320_int8dyn.onnx,
  SHA-256 d0a6c62f4bda6733f443b22bf9dce288b8f082ca0fc2f404a4931eb7cf0cbac2).
  A YOLOv8s PPE detector (classes Gloves, Helmet, No-Helmet, No-gloves,
  No-vest, Vest) trained by a university course project team, of which
  Zulfaqar Hafez was a member, with Ultralytics YOLOv8, then exported to ONNX
  at 320 px with dynamic int8 quantisation for the in-browser demo on
  zulfaqarhafez.com. Training code and evaluation:
  github.com/ZulfaqarHafez/AAI3001_Deep_Learning.
  Ultralytics YOLOv8 is licensed under AGPL-3.0. Check the Ultralytics licence
  terms before reusing the model.

Dataset and sample images
  "Personal Protective Equipment" v5, Roboflow Universe, workspace maxis,
  https://universe.roboflow.com/maxis/personal-protective-equipment-dtt2i-9qixs
  Licence: CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  src/ppe_bringup/samples/*.png are five images from its test split, as
  published on zulfaqarhafez.com (resized to a long side of 640 and WebP
  compressed there), converted to PNG here without other changes.
  src/ppe_bringup/samples/samples.json is the site's record of what the model
  finds in them. The annotated frames under docs/evidence/ are derived from
  these images.

Simulation assets
  The Gazebo demo loads the TurtleBot3 sandbox world, robot model, map and
  Nav2 parameters from the ROS packages nav2_minimal_tb3_sim and nav2_bringup
  (Apache-2.0) at launch time and modifies them in memory; none of their files
  are copied into this repository.

Code
  Pre- and post-processing are ported from src/components/demos/ppeDetect.ts
  and scripts/ppe-samples.py of the zulfaqarhafez.com site, by the same
  author. No licence file has been added to this repository yet.
